<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Milton Obote</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1925">1925</a>–<a href="/years/2005">2005</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Milton Obote was Uganda's first prime minister at independence in 1962 and later its president. In 1966 he suspended the constitution and sent troops against the palace of the kabaka of Buganda, Mutesa II, and in 1967 he abolished the kingdoms. Overthrown by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idi-amin">Idi Amin</a> in 1971, he returned to power in 1980 and was deposed again in 1985.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/milton-obote.jpg" alt="Milton Obote" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Warren K. Leffler · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:President_John_F._Kennedy_with_Prime_Minister_Milton_Obote_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
